["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Ducks beat you with their eyes. Hide from the eyes and you beat almost every duck.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view comparison. Left, a duck: its view covers about 360 degrees around it, 70 percent, with only a thin wedge in front seen by both eyes. Right, a person: about half the circle, with a wide zone in front seen by both eyes. Orange marks the zone seen by both eyes, where depth is judged best.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">What a duck sees: almost all around</text><path d=\"M110 150 L110.0 60.0 A90 90 0 1 1 109.8 60.0 Z\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\"/><path d=\"M110 150 L94.4 61.4 A90 90 0 0 1 125.6 61.4 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".8\"/><g transform=\"translate(110 150) rotate(-90)\"><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.7)\"><path d=\"M8 5.3999999999999995 L3 0.03 L-14 0.05 L-12 0.03 L-15 5.3999999999999995 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M8 -5.3999999999999995 L3 -0.03 L-14 -0.05 L-12 -0.03 L-15 -5.3999999999999995 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20.0\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M-17.0 -4.5 L-28.0 0 L-17.0 4.5 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"16.0\" y=\"-3.15\" width=\"14\" height=\"6.3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"30.0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M36.0 -2.5 L44.0 -2.0 L44.0 2.0 L36.0 2.5 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g></g><text x=\"110\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Duck: about 360° (70%)</text><path d=\"M300 150 L211.4 165.6 A90 90 0 1 1 388.6 165.6 Z\" fill=\"#e9e2d0\"/><path d=\"M300 150 L222.1 105.0 A90 90 0 0 1 377.9 105.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".5\"/><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"150\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#f6d7b0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">You: about half</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Both eyes: thin wedge</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Both eyes: wide</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Orange: seen by both eyes, best depth</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>A mallard sees almost all the way around <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>It can watch the whole sky without turning its head <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: field of view, and how sure we are</summary><ul><li>Ducks Unlimited describes a mallard's view as a full 360 degree circle <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>. A vision scientist quoted by hunting media calls ducks \"an extreme case\" of panoramic vision <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Ed Yong's book on animal senses, citing vision research, says the mallard field has no blind spot above or behind (60%, secondhand).</li><li>Some sources say there may be a small blind area right behind the head. Not settled: treat ducks as seeing everything (Tip).</li><li>Most waterfowl see each side with one eye. Only a thin zone in front is seen by both eyes <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Hunter meaning: there is no \"behind\" a duck. A circling flock sees your hide from every side (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Colour cones. A duck has four kinds: ultraviolet, blue, green and red, 75 percent. You have three: blue, green and red, with no ultraviolet. Ducks likely see ultraviolet light, 70 percent. Shine and glare stand out to them, a tip. Dull the gun, the face and the boat, a tip.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Colour: ducks have one more cone (75%)</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Duck</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">You</text><rect x=\"130\" y=\"50\" width=\"54\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8e6bbf\"/><text x=\"157\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">UV</text><rect x=\"130\" y=\"150\" width=\"54\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e9e2d0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M149 162 l16 16 M165 162 l-16 16\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/><rect x=\"194\" y=\"50\" width=\"54\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#3a6fb0\"/><text x=\"221\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Blue</text><rect x=\"194\" y=\"150\" width=\"54\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#3a6fb0\"/><rect x=\"258\" y=\"50\" width=\"54\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f8f4a\"/><text x=\"285\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Green</text><rect x=\"258\" y=\"150\" width=\"54\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f8f4a\"/><rect x=\"322\" y=\"50\" width=\"54\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Red</text><rect x=\"322\" y=\"150\" width=\"54\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"216\" width=\"380\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">They likely see ultraviolet light (70%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Shine and glare stand out to them (Tip)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dull the gun, the face and the boat (Tip)</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Four colour cones; you have three <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Shine and glare are your enemy (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what they see that you do not</summary><ul><li>Birds have an extra set of cones that pick up ultraviolet light: \"tetrachromatic\" vision (75%, Ducks Unlimited).</li><li>They see reds, yellows and blues more vividly than we do <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Ultraviolet helps them see well at dawn and dusk <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Feathers reflect ultraviolet. Young pintail drakes reflect it differently from adults <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Delta Waterfowl scientists say ducks likely see ultraviolet, and much is still unknown <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Hunter meaning: avoid shiny guns, glasses, phones, new plastic and a bare face. Some decoys use ultraviolet dulling paint; how much it matters is not proven (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation. Three ducks glide in toward decoys in front of a hide. Halfway in, the hunter lifts a bare, shiny face to look. The ducks flare, climb and fly away. End card: freeze until the shot, a tip.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">One face lifts: the whole flock flares</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"190\" width=\"400\" height=\"110\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".45\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"178\" width=\"80\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#9a8a5a\"/><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"186\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#6b6f4a\"/><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"3s\"/><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"174\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#f6d7b0\"/><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"174\" r=\"15\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ffe08a\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(220 230)\"><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-11\" cy=\"-3\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(264 231)\"><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-11\" cy=\"-3\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(308 232)\"><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-11\" cy=\"-3\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/></g><g><animateMotion dur=\"6s\" begin=\"0.0s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\" keyPoints=\"0;0.5;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;1\" calcMode=\"linear\" path=\"M390 50 C 320 70, 260 110, 210 160 C 200 140, 230 70, 380 40\"/><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(-1 1)\"><ellipse rx=\"4\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"13;4;13\" dur=\".4s\" repeatCount=\"15\"/></ellipse><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"0\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/></g></g><g><animateMotion dur=\"6s\" begin=\"0.2s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\" keyPoints=\"0;0.5;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;1\" calcMode=\"linear\" path=\"M390 50 C 320 70, 260 110, 210 160 C 200 140, 230 70, 380 40\"/><g transform=\"translate(-14 10) scale(-1 1)\"><ellipse rx=\"4\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"13;4;13\" dur=\".4s\" repeatCount=\"15\"/></ellipse><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"0\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/></g></g><g><animateMotion dur=\"6s\" begin=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\" keyPoints=\"0;0.5;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;1\" calcMode=\"linear\" path=\"M390 50 C 320 70, 260 110, 210 160 C 200 140, 230 70, 380 40\"/><g transform=\"translate(-28 20) scale(-1 1)\"><ellipse rx=\"4\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"13;4;13\" dur=\".4s\" repeatCount=\"15\"/></ellipse><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"0\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/></g></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"3.2s\" dur=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Face up!</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6.3s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"40\" y=\"252\" width=\"320\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Freeze until the shot (Tip)</text></g></svg>\n<figcaption>One face lifts: the whole flock flares. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two hides seen from the side with a duck circling above. Left, crossed: the hunter looks up with a shiny face in an open topped hide; the duck sees straight in. Right, ticked: the hunter keeps the head down under a brim and a cover roof; the duck sees only grass. Watch with your eyes, not your head, a tip.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">They look DOWN into your hide</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"200\" width=\"180\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".5\"/><rect x=\"40\" y=\"150\" width=\"120\" height=\"60\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#9a8a5a\"/><rect x=\"84\" y=\"160\" width=\"32\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#6b6f4a\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"148\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#f6d7b0\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"148\" r=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ffe08a\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><g transform=\"translate(140 62) scale(0.6) rotate(150)\"><path d=\"M8 5.3999999999999995 L3 26.4 L-14 44.0 L-12 26.4 L-15 5.3999999999999995 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M8 -5.3999999999999995 L3 -26.4 L-14 -44.0 L-12 -26.4 L-15 -5.3999999999999995 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"22.0\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M-19.0 -4.5 L-30.0 0 L-19.0 4.5 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"18.0\" y=\"-3.15\" width=\"14\" height=\"6.3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"32.0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M38.0 -2.5 L46.0 -2.0 L46.0 2.0 L38.0 2.5 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><line x1=\"132\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"104\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M32 252 l16 16 M48 252 l-16 16\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Face up, open top</text><rect x=\"210\" y=\"200\" width=\"180\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".5\"/><rect x=\"240\" y=\"150\" width=\"120\" height=\"60\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#9a8a5a\"/><path d=\"M238 150 Q300 120 362 150\" stroke=\"#7a6a3a\" stroke-width=\"10\" fill=\"none\"/><rect x=\"284\" y=\"160\" width=\"32\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#6b6f4a\"/><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"152\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#6b6f4a\"/><rect x=\"282\" y=\"140\" width=\"36\" height=\"6\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#4a4d33\"/><g transform=\"translate(340 62) scale(0.6) rotate(150)\"><path d=\"M8 5.3999999999999995 L3 26.4 L-14 44.0 L-12 26.4 L-15 5.3999999999999995 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M8 -5.3999999999999995 L3 -26.4 L-14 -44.0 L-12 -26.4 L-15 -5.3999999999999995 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"22.0\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M-19.0 -4.5 L-30.0 0 L-19.0 4.5 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"18.0\" y=\"-3.15\" width=\"14\" height=\"6.3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"32.0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M38.0 -2.5 L46.0 -2.0 L46.0 2.0 L38.0 2.5 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><line x1=\"332\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"304\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M232 260 l6 7 l12 -14\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"310\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Head down, roof</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Watch with your eyes, not your head (Tip)</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Bird eyes are built to catch motion <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>They look DOWN into your hide. Keep your head down (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why motion kills a hunt</summary><ul><li>Bird retinas keep blood vessels in one comb shaped structure (the pecten) instead of across the retina. That reduces visual clutter and helps them see motion <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Florida's wildlife agency: ducks have great eyesight and are very good at seeing movement; full camouflage and sitting still are the answer <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>No camouflage pattern hides a hunter who stares up or fidgets (Tip, widely reported).</li><li>Look with your eyes, not your face. Use a hat brim, a face mask or face paint (Tip).</li><li>Let one person call the shot. Everyone rises together, once (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/mallard-drake-flight.jpg\" alt=\"A mallard sees fine detail at 2 to 3 times your distance.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A mallard sees fine detail at 2 to 3 times your distance. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Bert de Tilly, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mallard_drake.03.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>They see fine detail 2.5 to 3 times farther than you <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>They judge depth by moving the head <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how they judge distance</summary><ul><li>With eyes on the sides, most of what a duck sees is flat. It bobs or turns its head to see an object from two angles, which builds depth <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Birds control the shape of both the cornea and the lens. Divers can see well under water <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Hunter meaning: a fake looking decoy spread, or a hide that sticks up, is seen from far out. Match the shape of the cover around you (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: the sun rises. Two hours before sunrise, nothing is legal. At 1 hour before sunrise, deer and grouse are legal, ducks and geese must wait. At 30 minutes before sunrise, ducks and geese are legal too. Then sunrise. In the evening deer end 1 hour after sunset and ducks end 30 minutes after sunset.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"190\" fill=\"#1f2a3a\"><animate attributeName=\"fill\" values=\"#1f2a3a;#5a6f8f;#a9c4de\" begin=\"0s\" dur=\"8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></rect>\n<circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"230\" r=\"26\" fill=\"#e8590c\"><animate attributeName=\"cy\" values=\"230;190;172\" keyTimes=\"0;0.85;1\" begin=\"0s\" dur=\"8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"190\" width=\"400\" height=\"110\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<path d=\"M0 190 Q 100 170 200 186 T 400 180 L400 196 L0 196 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"0s\" dur=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;0\" begin=\"2s\" dur=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2 hours before sunrise</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2s\" dur=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;0\" begin=\"4.5s\" dur=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1 hour before sunrise</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"4.5s\" dur=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;0\" begin=\"7s\" dur=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">30 minutes before sunrise</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"7s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sunrise</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"0s\" dur=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;0\" begin=\"2s\" dur=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"70\" width=\"340\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#c92a2a\" stroke=\"#c92a2a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Deer, grouse: wait</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"112\" width=\"340\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#c92a2a\" stroke=\"#c92a2a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"135\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ducks, geese: wait</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2s\" dur=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;0\" begin=\"4.5s\" dur=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"70\" width=\"340\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#5c7a3a\" stroke=\"#5c7a3a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Deer, grouse: GO</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"112\" width=\"340\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#c92a2a\" stroke=\"#c92a2a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"135\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ducks, geese: wait</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"4.5s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"70\" width=\"340\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#5c7a3a\" stroke=\"#5c7a3a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Deer, grouse: GO</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"112\" width=\"340\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#5c7a3a\" stroke=\"#5c7a3a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"135\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ducks, geese: GO</text></g>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ducks start 30 minutes later.</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Evenings: deer 1 hour after sunset,</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">ducks 30 minutes after.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Legal light for ducks starts 30 minutes before sunrise. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Ducks see well in low light and fly at night <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Most migration happens at night <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: low light facts</summary><ul><li>Ultraviolet sensitivity lets birds work fully at dawn and dusk <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Most waterfowl migrate at night. Movement picks up soon after sunset and peaks near midnight <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Under hunting pressure ducks fly out to feed at night <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Birds see a flickering light as flashes, where we see a steady light <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Legal hours for ducks: half an hour before sunrise to half an hour after sunset <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. See the <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds/17\">Rule Book</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hearing range on a scale from 20 hertz to 20 kilohertz. You hear about 20 hertz to 20 kilohertz. A mallard hears about 66 hertz to 7.6 kilohertz, 75 percent, small study. Best duck hearing is 1 to 3 kilohertz, near 2 kilohertz, and duck calls sit at 1 to 3 kilohertz, 75 percent. They hear a clank.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hearing: the call sits in the sweet spot</text><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"40.0\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"40.0\" y2=\"206\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"40.0\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">20 Hz</text><line x1=\"119.21660049141545\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"119.21660049141545\" y2=\"206\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"119.21660049141545\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100</text><line x1=\"232.5499338247488\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"232.5499338247488\" y2=\"206\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"232.5499338247488\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1 kHz</text><line x1=\"345.88326715808216\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"345.88326715808216\" y2=\"206\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"345.88326715808216\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10 kHz</text><rect x=\"40.0\" y=\"60\" width=\"340.0\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e9e2d0\"/><text x=\"153.33333333333331\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">You: 20 Hz to 20 kHz</text><rect x=\"98.76491318616058\" y=\"108\" width=\"233.6105610970779\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f6d7b0\"/><text x=\"214.99437835969792\" y=\"131\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Mallard: 66 Hz to 7.6 kHz</text><rect x=\"232.5499338247488\" y=\"156\" width=\"54.0737422015618\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"259.52849217934556\" y=\"179\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Best</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"240\" width=\"380\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Best hearing near 2 kHz; duck calls sit</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">at 1 to 3 kHz (75%). They hear a clank.</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Best hearing: 1 to 3 kHz, where duck calls sit <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>A clank or a slammed truck door carries (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what the studies found</summary><ul><li>A mallard hearing test (3 birds) found a range of about 66 Hz to 7.6 kHz, with best hearing near 2 kHz <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Mallards do not hear the very low sounds that pigeons do <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Ten diving bird species, including scaup and ruddy duck, shared their best hearing at 1 to 3 kHz. The ducks had the most sensitive hearing of the group <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Duck calls (their own voices) mostly sit in that same 1 to 3 kHz band <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Hunter meaning: a mouth call sits right in their best band. Call softly and rarely when birds are close (Tip).</li><li>Hunter meaning: metal on metal, a dog whistle or loud talk in the hide carries (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, top view of a J hook spread with the wind blowing left to right. Three ducks fly in from downwind, pass high over the spread, circle back, then turn and glide in against the wind, wings cupped, landing in the open pocket in front of the hide.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"200\" fill=\"#cfe0ea\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"240\" width=\"400\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"236\" width=\"70\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"185\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text><path d=\"M20 22 L110 22\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><polygon points=\"106,13 106,31 124,22\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"132\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">WIND</text><g transform=\"translate(70 200) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(55 180) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(52 158) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(62 138) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(84 128) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(100 208) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(118 214) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(78 214) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(110 120) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(140 110) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(172 104) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(205 100) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(238 98) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(270 98) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(302 100) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(334 104) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"168\" rx=\"58\" ry=\"32\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" opacity=\".5\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 5\"/><path d=\"M400 60 C 300 40, 160 40, 90 70 C 30 100, 60 150, 150 150 C 250 150, 360 160, 380 168 C 330 168, 280 168, 205 168\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 6\" opacity=\".5\"/><g><animateMotion dur=\"6.5s\" begin=\"0s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\" keyPoints=\"0;1\" keyTimes=\"0;1\" calcMode=\"linear\" path=\"M400 60 C 300 40, 160 40, 90 70 C 30 100, 60 150, 150 150 C 250 150, 360 160, 380 168 C 330 168, 280 168, 205 168\"/><g transform=\"translate(0 -14)\"><g transform=\"scale(1)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"14;4;14\" dur=\".5s\" repeatCount=\"12\"/><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"14;5\" begin=\"5.6s\" dur=\".6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></ellipse><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"0\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/></g></g></g><g><animateMotion dur=\"6.5s\" begin=\"0.25s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\" keyPoints=\"0;1\" keyTimes=\"0;1\" calcMode=\"linear\" path=\"M400 60 C 300 40, 160 40, 90 70 C 30 100, 60 150, 150 150 C 250 150, 360 160, 380 168 C 330 168, 280 168, 205 168\"/><g transform=\"translate(-6 0)\"><g transform=\"scale(1)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"14;4;14\" dur=\".5s\" repeatCount=\"12\"/><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"14;5\" begin=\"5.6s\" dur=\".6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></ellipse><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"0\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/></g></g></g><g><animateMotion dur=\"6.5s\" begin=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\" keyPoints=\"0;1\" keyTimes=\"0;1\" calcMode=\"linear\" path=\"M400 60 C 300 40, 160 40, 90 70 C 30 100, 60 150, 150 150 C 250 150, 360 160, 380 168 C 330 168, 280 168, 205 168\"/><g transform=\"translate(-12 14)\"><g transform=\"scale(1)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"14;4;14\" dur=\".5s\" repeatCount=\"12\"/><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"14;5\" begin=\"5.6s\" dur=\".6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></ellipse><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"0\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/></g></g></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;0\" begin=\"4.2s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"388\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">They circle, look</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6.8s\" dur=\".5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"232\" y=\"196\" width=\"160\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Land INTO the wind</text></g></svg>\n<figcaption>Ducks circle, then land into the wind. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Duck smell is barely studied. Do not count on it either way (Tip).</li><li>Wind matters because ducks land into it <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what we know about smell</summary><ul><li>The old belief that birds cannot smell is not supported. Reviews list ducks among birds with a working sense of smell <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>No study found here shows ducks avoid hunters by scent (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>). Ducks Unlimited and state agencies advise on sight and motion, not scent (Tip).</li><li>Wind still sets your hide: ducks land into the wind, so set the spread with the wind at your back or side (80% for landing into wind; the setup is a Tip).</li><li>Old hand's rule (opinion): \"Play the wind for the landing, not for the nose.\"</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Four mallards asleep in a row on the water. The two at the ends keep one eye open, facing out, away from the group. The two in the middle shut both eyes more. In a study, edge birds slept with one eye open about 32 percent of the time, middle birds about 12 percent, 75 percent. A sleeping raft still has lookouts, 80 percent.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sleeping with one eye open (80%)</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"150\" width=\"400\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".5\"/><g transform=\"translate(70 150) scale(-1.3 1.3)\"><path d=\"M-30 0 Q-34 -14 -18 -14 L10 -12 Q24 -10 24 0 Q20 10 -2 10 L-22 10 Q-32 8 -30 0Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M10 -10 Q12 -18 16 -22 L22 -18 Q18 -12 18 -6 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-22\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -24 L35 -20 L24 -18 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><circle cx=\"47\" cy=\"121\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"47\" cy=\"121\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"39\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"12.6\" y2=\"74.8\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"9.0,70.0 10.8,82.4 20.4,75.2\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><g transform=\"translate(160 150) scale(1.3)\"><path d=\"M-30 0 Q-34 -14 -18 -14 L10 -12 Q24 -10 24 0 Q20 10 -2 10 L-22 10 Q-32 8 -30 0Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M10 -10 Q12 -18 16 -22 L22 -18 Q18 -12 18 -6 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-22\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -24 L35 -20 L24 -18 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><line x1=\"179\" y1=\"121\" x2=\"187\" y2=\"121\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><g transform=\"translate(250 150) scale(1.3)\"><path d=\"M-30 0 Q-34 -14 -18 -14 L10 -12 Q24 -10 24 0 Q20 10 -2 10 L-22 10 Q-32 8 -30 0Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M10 -10 Q12 -18 16 -22 L22 -18 Q18 -12 18 -6 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-22\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -24 L35 -20 L24 -18 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><line x1=\"269\" y1=\"121\" x2=\"277\" y2=\"121\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><g transform=\"translate(340 150) scale(1.3)\"><path d=\"M-30 0 Q-34 -14 -18 -14 L10 -12 Q24 -10 24 0 Q20 10 -2 10 L-22 10 Q-32 8 -30 0Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M10 -10 Q12 -18 16 -22 L22 -18 Q18 -12 18 -6 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-22\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -24 L35 -20 L24 -18 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><circle cx=\"363\" cy=\"121\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"363\" cy=\"121\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"371\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"397.4\" y2=\"74.8\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"401.0,70.0 389.6,75.2 399.2,82.4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Edge: eye out</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Edge: eye out</text><text x=\"205\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Middle: both eyes shut more</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"222\" width=\"380\" height=\"70\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Edge birds: one eye open about 32% of sleep</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Middle birds: about 12% (75%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A sleeping raft still has lookouts</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Edge ducks sleep with one eye open, facing out <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Half the brain stays awake <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the study</summary><ul><li>Mallards sleeping in a row of four: the two edge birds slept with one eye open about 32% of the time, the middle birds about 12% <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The open eye faced away from the group, where a predator would come from. The awake half of the brain reacted fast to threats <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>This is called unihemispheric sleep <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Hunter meaning: a sleeping raft is never fully asleep. Sneaks on rafted ducks rarely work in the open (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Sense</th><th>Strength</th><th>Beat it (Tip)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Eyes</td><td>Near 360°, motion, ultraviolet</td><td>Still, head down, no shine, roof on hide</td></tr><tr><td>Ears</td><td>Best at 1 to 3 kHz</td><td>Quiet gear, soft calls</td></tr><tr><td>Nose</td><td>Not well known</td><td>Ignore; play the wind for landing</td></tr><tr><td>Lookouts</td><td>One eye open at the edges</td><td>Do not sneak open water rafts</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the 40 year hunter's checklist (opinion)</summary><ul><li>Face covered or painted, gloves on, nothing shiny.</li><li>Hide matches the cover around it and has a roof or brim.</li><li>Eyes move, head does not. One caller, one \"take them\" call.</li><li>Gear packed quiet: no loose shells rattling, no metal on metal.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Hook</th><th>Means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>\"No behind on a duck\"</td><td>Near 360° view <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></td></tr><tr><td>\"Four cones, no shine\"</td><td>Ultraviolet vision <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr><tr><td>\"Eyes move, head stays\"</td><td>Beat motion (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>2 kHz</td><td>Best duck hearing <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr><tr><td>32 vs 12</td><td>Percent one eye sleep, edge vs middle <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Old hand's rule (opinion, widely taught): \"If you can see the duck's eye, it can see yours.\"</p></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li>\"Glare scares.\" Shine is seen from far off (Tip).</li><li>\"Ducks fly at night, so the morning lake can change.\" Night migration <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Topic</th><th>Main source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vision</td><td>Ducks Unlimited, Delta Waterfowl</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing</td><td>Mallard audiogram, USGS study</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Rattenborg and others, 1999</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source, with date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.ducks.org/conservation/waterfowl-research-science/a-birds-eye-view\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited, A bird's eye view</a>: 360 degree window, 2.5 to 3 times detail, cones, ultraviolet, pecten, flicker, head movement for depth. Read directly 2026-10-11 (70 to 75%).</li><li><a href=\"https://deltawaterfowl.org/what-do-ducks-see\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Delta Waterfowl, What do ducks see?</a>: likely ultraviolet, much unknown. Search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.outdoorlife.com/blogs/master-class/2013/10/how-ducks-see-science-behind-waterfowl-eyesight.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outdoor Life, how ducks see</a> and <a href=\"https://www.grandviewoutdoors.com/big-game-hunting/whitetail-deer/new-sitka-waterfowl-apparel-features-revolutionary-camo-pattern\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Grand View Outdoors on panoramic vision</a>: scientist quotes. Search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Ed Yong, An Immense World, mallard visual field (reader note): no blind spot. Secondhand, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://myfwc.com/hunting/waterfowl/hunt-guide/hunt-tips/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Florida Fish and Wildlife Conservation Commission, waterfowl hunt tips</a>: eyesight, movement, landing into wind. Search preview 2026-10-11 (75 to 80%).</li><li><a href=\"https://link.springer.com/doi/10.1007/s00359-017-1204-6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mallard audiogram, Journal of Comparative Physiology A (2017)</a>: 66 Hz to 7.6 kHz, best near 2 kHz. Search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.usgs.gov/publications/comparison-auditory-brainstem-responses-across-diving-bird-species\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">USGS, auditory brainstem responses across diving bird species</a>: best at 1 to 3 kHz, calls in the same band. Search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://scholars.okstate.edu/en/publications/facultative-control-of-avian-unihemispheric-sleep-under-the-risk-/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Rattenborg and others, unihemispheric sleep under the risk of predation (1999)</a> and <a href=\"https://scientificamerican.com/article/meet-the-animals-that-literally-sleep-with-one-eye-open\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Scientific American</a>. Search preview 2026-10-11 (75 to 80%).</li><li><a href=\"https://ducks.org/conservation/waterfowl-research-science/ducks-after-dark\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited, Ducks after dark</a>: night migration and feeding. Read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/neuroanatomy/articles/10.3389/fnana.2015.00102/full\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Frontiers in Neuroanatomy review on bird olfaction (2015)</a> and <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2692081\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">review on the anosmia myth</a>: birds do smell. Search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul></details>"]